---
alwaysApply: true
---

## Blade / Views

- **Never** use `@php` / `@endphp` or inline `<?php ?>` in Blade for logic.
- Blade is for presentation only (`@if`, `@foreach`, `{{ }}`). Compute data in controllers, models, helpers, or ViewModels — pass ready-to-use variables to the view.
- **Never** write `<style>` blocks inside Blade templates.
- **Never** use inline `style=""` attributes. Always express styles as classes in the appropriate CSS file.

## JavaScript

- JavaScript is a **progressive enhancement tool**, not an application layer.
- Allowed: DOM helpers, UI library initialization (modals, charts, date pickers), isolated micro-interactions.
- Not allowed: application state management, business logic, API orchestration, or any data that duplicates server state.
- **Do not duplicate Livewire component state in JavaScript.** If the data lives on a Livewire component, it is the single source of truth — JS must not maintain its own copy.
- Communicate between Livewire and JS via browser events (see Livewire rules). Never reach into Livewire internals from JS.

## Frontend Assets

- All custom CSS must live in `public/custom/` using the naming pattern `custom-{name}.css`
  (e.g. `public/custom/custom-dashboard.css`, `public/custom/custom-auth.css`).
- One file per feature or page. Do not create a single monolithic `custom.css`.
- Link the stylesheet using the `asset()` helper, placed in the `@section('styles')` stack or
  equivalent layout slot — never hardcoded in a component or partial:
  ```blade
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('custom/custom-{name}.css') }}">
  ```
- CSS in these files must use the design system token variables (`var(--color-*)`, `var(--shadow-*)`, etc.)
  and follow the `ui-` class prefix convention.
- Refer to `.cursor/rules/design.md` for the full design system and token reference.
